  "description": "Realistic password strength estimation for .NET: a faithful, modern port of the zxcvbn-ts (Dropbox zxcvbn) algorithm. Instead of composition rules (uppercase + digit + symbol), Zxcvbn scores what attackers actually try. It matches passwords against ranked frequency dictionaries (common passwords, English words, names, surnames, wikipedia, diceware, word sequences) including reversed and l33t-substituted variants, keyboard spatial walks (qwerty, azerty, qwertz, dvorak, keypads), repeats, sequences, recent-year regexes and dates in many formats, then runs the exact minimum-guess dynamic-programming search to produce a 0 to 4 score, guess counts, four crack-time scenarios with human-readable strings, the full match sequence and actionable feedback. Custom user inputs (username, email, app name) and custom dictionaries, l33t tables and keyboard graphs are supported. Thread-safe, zero external dependencies, aligned with NIST 800-63B guidance to check passwords against strength lists rather than composition rules.",
